Now let me write a shared price-row parser/upsert helper used by both import and reprice. Actually the import and reprice both need to parse+upsert a price row. Let me create a `PriceRowWriter` that, given (em, repo), upserts a price row from a validated array, returning the PriceRow. Both import and reprice will use it.

Let me create `PriceRowWriter`:

```php
final class PriceRowWriter
{
    public function __construct(private BillingRepository $repo, private EntityManagerInterface $em) {}

    /**
     * @param array{provider:string, model:string, valid_from:string, unit:string, currency?:string, rates:array<string,string>} $raw
     */
    public function upsert(array $raw): PriceRow
    {
        $providerCode = self::requireString($raw, 'provider');
        $modelCode = self::requireString($raw, 'model');
        $validFrom = IsoDateTime::parseUtc(self::requireString($raw, 'valid_from'));
        $unit = self::requireString($raw, 'unit');
        if (!Unit::isValid($unit)) throw new DomainException(...);
        $currency = ($raw['currency'] ?? 'USD');
        $ratesRaw = self::requireArray($raw, 'rates');
        $rates = self::parseRates($unit, $ratesRaw);

        $provider = $this->repo->findProviderByCode($providerCode);
        if (null === $provider) throw new DomainException('Неизвестный провайдер: '.code);
        $model = $this->repo->findModelByProviderCodeAndCode($providerCode, $modelCode);
        if (null === $model) throw new DomainException('Неизвестная модель...');

        $row = $this->repo->findPriceRow($providerCode, $modelCode, $validFrom) ?? new PriceRow();
        if (null === $row->getId()) $this->em->persist($row);
        $row->setProvider($provider); $row->setModel($model); $row->setValidFrom($validFrom);
        $row->setCurrency($currency); $row->setUnit($unit);
        $row->replaceRates($rates);

        return $row;
    }
}
```

